@startuml
' Figure 24.6  Expiry and supersession
' Reading order: top to bottom. A memory is written with a source and
' a TTL by its type. While it lives it may be renewed by new evidence,
' superseded by a newer memory or by a record of fact, or reach its
' expiry. Only a live memory is read, and then as evidence. From
' memory.store, memory.supersede, and knowops.expiry.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
hide empty description
[*] --> Live : Written with source, TTL by type
Live --> Live : Renewed by new evidence
Live --> Superseded : Newer memory or record of fact
Live --> Expired : TTL reached
Superseded --> [*]
Expired --> [*]
@enduml
